1
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:05,760
The next one's on its way, we play!

2
00:00:06,660 --> 00:00:07,490
Aaaaah!

3
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:15,750
Parry!

4
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:26,266
The more time I can buy, the
better chance they have to escape.

5
00:00:26,680 --> 00:00:30,445
I'm just going to run around and
parry every single thing I see!

6
00:00:36,580 --> 00:00:38,440
I was finally able to stop!

7
00:00:43,980 --> 00:00:44,810
What?

8
00:00:45,020 --> 00:00:46,255
Who's this old-timer?

9
00:00:57,260 --> 00:00:59,957
I love the world.

10
00:01:00,040 --> 00:01:02,857
I love the world. I

11
00:01:02,940 --> 00:01:09,940
don't

12
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:11,470
think

13
00:01:11,553 --> 00:01:13,860
I can trust.

14
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:16,277
I love my inspiration.

15
00:01:16,360 --> 00:01:17,877
I don't know.

16
00:01:17,960 --> 00:01:20,837
What I want to know?

17
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:22,237
What I want to know?

18
00:01:22,320 --> 00:01:24,177
What I want to know?

19
00:01:24,260 --> 00:01:29,617
Let's go back to the end of the day.

20
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:34,900
If it's back to the end of the day,

21
00:01:37,380 --> 00:01:40,520
I won't be able to reach
the end of the day.

22
00:01:41,260 --> 00:01:43,317
Let's go back to the end of the day.

23
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:46,180
Let's go back to the end of the day.

24
00:02:21,940 --> 00:02:23,646
Sparkly gold armor and sword?

25
00:02:24,160 --> 00:02:26,925
Even the horse has a
whole sparkly gold outfit.

26
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:30,793
Why would he be standing in
a war zone looking all fancy?

27
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:33,433
Maybe the poor guy is lost or something.

28
00:02:34,540 --> 00:02:35,480
Huh? Huh?

29
00:02:37,340 --> 00:02:38,170
Whatever.

30
00:02:38,820 --> 00:02:41,291
Now's not the time to get distracted, Nor.

31
00:02:46,660 --> 00:02:48,957
I won't stand a chance
if these soldiers gather

32
00:02:49,040 --> 00:02:51,628
up their weapons and
come at me all at once.

33
00:02:52,660 --> 00:02:56,836
I'll have to keep parrying them, keep
their weapons out of their hands.

34
00:02:57,900 --> 00:03:00,724
Not sure what that is,
but I'm gonna get it too.

35
00:03:14,280 --> 00:03:17,817
I still can't help but wonder what
this old guy's doing out here.

36
00:03:17,900 --> 00:03:19,497
What the devil just happened?

37
00:03:19,580 --> 00:03:20,410
Oh, right.

38
00:03:20,493 --> 00:03:23,636
I can't give the soldiers
time to pick up their stuff.

39
00:03:33,180 --> 00:03:37,415
I also gotta remember to breathe every
once in a while or I'll pass out.

40
00:03:37,880 --> 00:03:39,527
Wait a second, were you not?

41
00:03:42,260 --> 00:03:43,640
He's going to kill me.

42
00:03:43,820 --> 00:03:46,600
Does the sparkly old man, does he know me?

43
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:49,660
Nah, we've never met before.

44
00:03:51,220 --> 00:03:53,040
But jeez, he's crazy.

45
00:03:53,300 --> 00:03:55,006
He's gonna get hurt out here.

46
00:03:55,460 --> 00:03:58,401
Well, I guess he does have
a sword if he needs it.

47
00:04:00,080 --> 00:04:01,260
Stay focused, Noor.

48
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:03,913
You've just got to keep doing your part.

49
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:34,306
Pretty sure that sparkly gold old man is
going to get hurt if he stays out here?

50
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:37,997
Please, you must tell me who you are?

51
00:04:38,080 --> 00:04:40,320
And why haven't you killed me yet?

52
00:04:41,260 --> 00:04:44,380
Oh, the poor guy thinks I
came here to take him out?

53
00:04:46,280 --> 00:04:48,660
Well, I guess I can't really blame him.

54
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:52,060
Not that weapon.

55
00:04:52,620 --> 00:04:53,780
No, don't be.

56
00:04:54,700 --> 00:04:56,657
I don't want him to be afraid of me.

57
00:04:56,740 --> 00:05:00,980
I need to do something to reassure
him, to let him know I'm not hostile.

58
00:05:04,520 --> 00:05:06,120
Is this working?

59
00:05:12,500 --> 00:05:14,140
Nope, guess not.

60
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:15,718
Didn't work at all.

61
00:05:24,400 --> 00:05:25,740
I'm getting tired.

62
00:05:26,740 --> 00:05:29,377
I've really been going
non-stop this whole time.

63
00:05:29,460 --> 00:05:33,166
And Low Heel can't do anything
to relieve exhaustion like this.

64
00:05:39,780 --> 00:05:45,040
Lynn, Inez, Rolo, I
hope you get out safely.

65
00:05:47,480 --> 00:05:48,840
Shooting Star!

66
00:05:56,740 --> 00:05:58,180
That skill.

67
00:06:06,140 --> 00:06:07,400
Drag race.

68
00:06:14,060 --> 00:06:19,820
It's you good to see you grill grizzly?

69
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:25,260
or glibbery? It's Gilbert.

70
00:06:29,220 --> 00:06:30,620
You did all this?

71
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:36,220
Nice of you to finally join us, Master.

72
00:06:37,020 --> 00:06:37,850
Sorry.

73
00:06:39,020 --> 00:06:40,880
Wait, you're the...

74
00:06:44,020 --> 00:06:46,800
I do not know who you are, but thank you.

75
00:06:47,740 --> 00:06:49,540
We will take care of the rest.

76
00:06:52,620 --> 00:06:54,800
We must at least handle the clean-up,

77
00:06:55,020 --> 00:06:58,667
or to abstain the honor of the
6th Troop of the Royal Capital.

78
00:07:05,640 --> 00:07:06,760
Thousand Blades!

79
00:07:09,960 --> 00:07:11,477
I remember! That's...

80
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:14,000
that's the power of the swordsman!

81
00:07:14,380 --> 00:07:16,556
The one I've always dreamed of being!

82
00:07:22,380 --> 00:07:23,417
Oh, dear.

83
00:07:23,500 --> 00:07:26,577
And after I warned him
against any excessive killing.

84
00:07:26,660 --> 00:07:27,490
Oh-ho-ho!

85
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:29,565
That's a tall order, isn't it?

86
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:32,781
Especially when we're faced
with such a vast army.

87
00:07:33,380 --> 00:07:36,257
Well, corpses will not
provide us any needed intel.

88
00:07:36,340 --> 00:07:39,197
I find the living to be
immensely more cooperative.

89
00:07:39,280 --> 00:07:43,868
Especially after bringing back missing
limbs over and over with healing magic.

90
00:07:44,860 --> 00:07:45,690
Hmm.

91
00:07:45,773 --> 00:07:46,603
That's a joke.

92
00:07:46,686 --> 00:07:49,988
Well, it doesn't quite sound
like a joke whenever you say it.

93
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:53,480
Okun, they should be
arriving any minute now.

94
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:54,830
Be ready.

95
00:07:55,160 --> 00:07:56,454
Don't have to tell me.

96
00:07:56,640 --> 00:08:00,405
We have been strung along by the
enemy long enough for my taste.

97
00:08:00,740 --> 00:08:02,460
Now it's my time to shine.

98
00:08:24,080 --> 00:08:26,600
Oh-ho, their eyes are as red as fire.

99
00:08:26,860 --> 00:08:28,917
You seem to be enjoying this, Oaken.

100
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:30,000
But of course,

101
00:08:30,380 --> 00:08:34,792
a good battle is always riveting no
matter how long in the tooth I may get.

102
00:08:35,180 --> 00:08:37,820
Now, shall we add the final touches?

103
00:08:40,840 --> 00:08:41,880
Soul prison!

104
00:08:52,180 --> 00:08:54,280
It's our turn now. Let's go.

105
00:08:57,380 --> 00:09:01,262
Time to save all the survivors and
make them turn over a new leaf.

106
00:09:03,900 --> 00:09:04,730
Oh, wow.

107
00:09:05,060 --> 00:09:08,707
They're the instructors who
taught me at the training schools.

108
00:09:14,100 --> 00:09:16,860
I can't believe I'm
getting to see them again.

109
00:09:22,180 --> 00:09:23,137
Hang on!

110
00:09:23,220 --> 00:09:24,620
Is that?

111
00:09:26,260 --> 00:09:27,217
It is.

112
00:09:27,300 --> 00:09:28,480
That's Noor.

113
00:09:35,500 --> 00:09:37,320
Thanks a lot, Lin.

114
00:09:38,120 --> 00:09:39,826
I'm feeling a lot better now.

115
00:09:40,440 --> 00:09:42,793
All right, but are you sure you're okay?

116
00:09:42,960 --> 00:09:45,320
You should really rest a little longer.

117
00:09:45,700 --> 00:09:47,406
Nah, I've gotten enough rest.

118
00:09:47,640 --> 00:09:49,522
I think I can move around again.

119
00:09:49,760 --> 00:09:51,560
I am really hungry, though.

120
00:09:52,540 --> 00:09:55,717
A commanding officer confessed
under Sane's interrogation.

121
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:57,271
They have no more troops.

122
00:09:57,500 --> 00:10:00,357
They already threw everything
at us, including the dragon,

123
00:10:00,440 --> 00:10:03,557
as well as all the other beasts
that attacked the capital.

124
00:10:03,640 --> 00:10:06,097
But I'm afraid the Emperor has escaped.

125
00:10:06,180 --> 00:10:07,240
The Emperor?

126
00:10:07,600 --> 00:10:11,860
That decrepit old fogey showed up
here on the battlefield? He did.

127
00:10:12,140 --> 00:10:14,964
He must have been very
confident in his chances.

128
00:10:16,220 --> 00:10:20,044
Dumb move for a guy who demands
his people call him a wise ruler.

129
00:10:20,400 --> 00:10:22,929
That old geezer must
be losing his marbles.

130
00:10:23,160 --> 00:10:24,040
Old geezer?

131
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:25,965
That terrified old gray fella?

132
00:10:26,620 --> 00:10:27,460
Hold on.

133
00:10:27,780 --> 00:10:30,177
Do you know who we're
talking about, young man?

134
00:10:30,260 --> 00:10:31,090
I think.

135
00:10:31,173 --> 00:10:32,180
I just met a guy.

136
00:10:33,040 --> 00:10:36,357
He was riding a horse all
decked out in sparkly gold gear.

137
00:10:36,440 --> 00:10:38,077
I mean, he was hard to miss.

138
00:10:38,160 --> 00:10:39,513
Gold on his horse, huh?

139
00:10:40,020 --> 00:10:43,080
He must have been employing
Orichalcum's saddlery.

140
00:10:43,880 --> 00:10:48,527
That's very high-grade equipment that
can support an extensive array of skills.

141
00:10:48,640 --> 00:10:52,160
In which case, it makes sense
how he escaped so quickly.

142
00:10:53,020 --> 00:10:58,200
But seriously wearing all gold, his
fashion sense is as shabby as his attitude.

143
00:10:58,580 --> 00:11:01,874
If he escapes across the
border, we cannot go after him.

144
00:11:02,180 --> 00:11:06,197
There's a fortress and a heavily
guarded bridge that spans the ravine.

145
00:11:06,280 --> 00:11:09,986
There's no hope of catching up
to him by now with normal means.

146
00:11:10,100 --> 00:11:15,040
If only there was a way for us all to
fly together somehow. You know what?

147
00:11:15,480 --> 00:11:17,833
I think that might actually be possible.

148
00:11:18,580 --> 00:11:19,920
What do you mean, son?

149
00:11:22,460 --> 00:11:23,437
Well, I guess.

150
00:11:23,520 --> 00:11:25,344
Assuming that it's still alive.

151
00:11:29,820 --> 00:11:33,317
What an incredible sight
to behold being able to

152
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:35,777
see a legendary creature
up close and personal!

153
00:11:35,860 --> 00:11:39,277
Like this this makes living
to my old age worth it.

154
00:11:39,360 --> 00:11:44,184
Same here this must be the first time I've
ever been tasked with healing a dragon?

155
00:11:56,660 --> 00:11:57,940
Well, well, Noor.

156
00:11:58,320 --> 00:12:01,380
You've really grown quite
a lot, haven't you? Hmm?

157
00:12:01,820 --> 00:12:03,291
I didn't know it was you.

158
00:12:04,320 --> 00:12:05,150
Pardon?

159
00:12:05,233 --> 00:12:06,063
This man?

160
00:12:06,146 --> 00:12:08,820
Is Noor you say? That's right.

161
00:12:09,040 --> 00:12:11,511
It took me a few minutes to recognize him.

162
00:12:11,740 --> 00:12:12,570
Yeah.

163
00:12:12,653 --> 00:12:15,660
Been a while since I've seen you. Ho-ho!

164
00:12:16,080 --> 00:12:18,900
I hadn't the slightest
idea it was you at all.

165
00:12:19,140 --> 00:12:21,669
And you're much larger
than you used to be.

166
00:12:21,860 --> 00:12:23,917
I'm glad to see that you're still alive.

167
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:25,260
Excuse me?

168
00:12:25,680 --> 00:12:28,504
That is not a very nice
thing to say now, is it?

169
00:12:28,660 --> 00:12:33,131
It is well within my abilities to live
another hundred years or more easily.

170
00:12:33,640 --> 00:12:35,800
And you're still funny, too, I see.

171
00:12:36,040 --> 00:12:38,100
I am not telling you a joke.

172
00:12:41,200 --> 00:12:44,040
But listen, Nor, are you sure about this?

173
00:12:44,760 --> 00:12:49,080
Humans riding on the back of a dragon
seems like a terrible idea to me.

174
00:12:50,580 --> 00:12:51,657
Don't worry about that.

175
00:12:51,740 --> 00:12:53,460
We've got Rolo with us.

176
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:54,830
Huh?

177
00:12:56,940 --> 00:13:01,620
Well now, Rolo, my boy, are you
confident in this ability of yours?

178
00:13:03,340 --> 00:13:04,170
No, sir.

179
00:13:04,380 --> 00:13:06,040
I have no confidence at all.

180
00:13:06,800 --> 00:13:07,760
Oh, ho, ho.

181
00:13:09,120 --> 00:13:10,057
You'll be okay.

182
00:13:10,140 --> 00:13:11,680
You can do this, Rolo.

183
00:13:15,440 --> 00:13:17,499
It seems our dragon is coming, too.

184
00:13:17,960 --> 00:13:18,920
Um, yes, okay.

185
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:22,438
Are you absolutely sure we
should be riding a dragon?

186
00:13:22,660 --> 00:13:23,490
Of course.

187
00:13:23,573 --> 00:13:24,481
Go for it, Rolo.

188
00:13:25,600 --> 00:13:26,440
Um, okay.

189
00:13:38,340 --> 00:13:39,460
Oh, man.

190
00:13:39,740 --> 00:13:41,034
Seems like it's angry.

191
00:13:42,060 --> 00:13:43,120
You can tell?

192
00:13:44,040 --> 00:13:45,317
Only from how it sounds.

193
00:13:45,400 --> 00:13:47,753
I've lived in the mountains for a while.

194
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:51,240
And wants to get revenge
against those who hurt it.

195
00:13:52,020 --> 00:13:54,314
He would like you to order it to do so.

196
00:13:54,820 --> 00:13:55,650
What now?

197
00:13:55,940 --> 00:13:59,360
You have that much communication
with this large dragon?

198
00:13:59,940 --> 00:14:00,770
Extraordinary!

199
00:14:00,853 --> 00:14:02,152
It's just extraordinary!

200
00:14:02,780 --> 00:14:04,700
Yeah, Rolo is a superstar.

201
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:07,040
No, I'm really not.

202
00:14:07,340 --> 00:14:09,660
This dragon thinks Norris...

203
00:14:13,120 --> 00:14:15,200
It says it's ready to go now.

204
00:14:15,740 --> 00:14:16,570
All right.

205
00:14:16,720 --> 00:14:19,040
If you're going, get ready. Okay.

206
00:14:23,380 --> 00:14:25,556
You guys are going with them as well?

207
00:14:26,380 --> 00:14:27,210
Yes.

208
00:14:27,293 --> 00:14:29,377
Rolo is the only one who
can speak to the dragon.

209
00:14:29,460 --> 00:14:31,880
So he'll need as much help as he can get.

210
00:14:32,280 --> 00:14:33,997
Ines and I will go to guard him.

211
00:14:34,080 --> 00:14:35,962
You'll be joining us too, right?

212
00:14:36,780 --> 00:14:37,610
Wait, what?

213
00:14:40,040 --> 00:14:41,940
Oh, I guess I could.

214
00:14:44,980 --> 00:14:47,860
But, well, I'm really
not good with heights.

215
00:14:49,160 --> 00:14:51,500
I am the one who came up with the idea,

216
00:14:51,680 --> 00:14:55,800
and I dragged Rolo into this, so it
would be awkward now if I didn't.

217
00:14:57,160 --> 00:14:59,740
But still, I mean...

218
00:15:02,500 --> 00:15:05,640
Okay, sure, I'm going to.

219
00:15:06,540 --> 00:15:07,820
Thank you so much!

220
00:15:08,260 --> 00:15:10,907
Having you is like the
strength of a hundred!

221
00:15:11,120 --> 00:15:12,280
I'm coming as well.

222
00:15:13,400 --> 00:15:15,880
I must continue to look after my patient.

223
00:15:16,500 --> 00:15:19,265
Besides, I believe we
have a duty to diplomacy.

224
00:15:19,900 --> 00:15:21,040
Isn't that right?

225
00:15:21,940 --> 00:15:23,640
Don't lump me in with you.

226
00:15:23,840 --> 00:15:27,220
I do not try to intimidate
people with childish mischief.

227
00:15:27,860 --> 00:15:29,120
Wow, you're the...

228
00:15:32,380 --> 00:15:33,460
Thief instructor!

229
00:15:33,840 --> 00:15:35,075
So you're coming too?

230
00:15:35,300 --> 00:15:36,220
I am.

231
00:15:36,440 --> 00:15:41,380
If you're going to fly on this giant beast,
then you'll need the concealment skill.

232
00:15:41,680 --> 00:15:43,092
I can take care of that.

233
00:15:43,740 --> 00:15:44,840
Yes, good point.

234
00:15:45,540 --> 00:15:47,128
All right, I'm coming, too.

235
00:15:47,480 --> 00:15:50,800
Oaken, do you not need to
supervise the stone cage?

236
00:15:51,620 --> 00:15:52,660
Okay, fine.

237
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:55,200
I will go as well.

238
00:15:56,080 --> 00:16:00,160
I believe you will be in need of
a negotiator. Father! Brother!

239
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:02,640
I'm so glad you're safe!

240
00:16:03,540 --> 00:16:06,128
I guess you've been
pretty worried about us.

241
00:16:06,480 --> 00:16:08,598
I'm glad to see you're safe as well.

242
00:16:09,840 --> 00:16:12,605
You chose to return
instead of going to Mithra.

243
00:16:13,140 --> 00:16:17,081
Yes, I'm willing to accept my
punishment for disobeying your order.

244
00:16:17,880 --> 00:16:18,710
No need.

245
00:16:19,040 --> 00:16:22,511
It was my own fault for giving
you such an idiotic command.

246
00:16:23,920 --> 00:16:25,979
I'm relieved you made it back here.

247
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:34,360
Now, Rain, you are in charge of
making any judgment calls out there.

248
00:16:35,580 --> 00:16:37,080
Also, Sir Noor.

249
00:16:38,440 --> 00:16:41,900
I apologize for always asking, but please.

250
00:16:42,480 --> 00:16:43,715
Take care of my kids.

251
00:16:44,660 --> 00:16:46,760
Sure, don't even worry about it.

252
00:16:46,940 --> 00:16:48,528
We'll get them back safely.

253
00:16:49,100 --> 00:16:50,480
I'm counting on you.

254
00:16:56,760 --> 00:16:57,590
Okay.

255
00:16:58,160 --> 00:16:58,990
Now fly.

256
00:17:08,520 --> 00:17:10,579
Are you sure you're okay with this?

257
00:17:12,160 --> 00:17:15,101
I mean, shouldn't you have
said something to Noor?

258
00:17:16,560 --> 00:17:19,100
We just finally found him after all.

259
00:17:20,240 --> 00:17:24,420
Fact is, he never really needed
us to play a role in his life.

260
00:17:25,220 --> 00:17:28,749
The idea that we would be able
to take him in and raise him?

261
00:17:29,240 --> 00:17:31,100
We were showing our hubris.

262
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:33,412
Yeah, right, no kidding.

263
00:17:33,640 --> 00:17:36,699
He was like a hero born
straight out of the legends.

264
00:17:36,840 --> 00:17:38,400
I feel pretty silly.

265
00:17:39,540 --> 00:17:40,800
Right now I

266
00:17:45,960 --> 00:17:48,840
I am deeply ashamed of my own laziness.

267
00:17:51,060 --> 00:17:55,942
I should not have been wasting time thinking
I was in any position to teach others!

268
00:17:56,600 --> 00:18:00,557
I am going to retrain myself
from the beginning now

269
00:18:00,640 --> 00:18:02,817
that I've been made aware
of my own shortcomings.

270
00:18:02,900 --> 00:18:06,480
I cannot rest on my laurels
and let my sword rust.

271
00:18:07,700 --> 00:18:11,171
For a guy who's deeply ashamed,
you seem pretty darn happy.

272
00:18:11,400 --> 00:18:15,500
But of course, just think of
the spectacle he showed us.

273
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:17,720
Yeah, got that right.

274
00:18:18,020 --> 00:18:21,200
After seeing something
like that, who wouldn't be?

275
00:18:32,220 --> 00:18:36,677
found anything nothing any luck

276
00:18:36,760 --> 00:18:40,780
there lady Lindbergh not a thing

277
00:18:50,500 --> 00:18:52,088
He's faster than I thought.

278
00:18:52,700 --> 00:18:56,340
Worst case, he may have already
arrived back at the Empire.

279
00:18:59,920 --> 00:19:04,273
Beyond that steel bridge, the land
turns into Empire-controlled territory.

280
00:19:04,360 --> 00:19:06,478
We cannot just wildly rush in there.

281
00:19:07,040 --> 00:19:11,275
I know we've come a long way, but
perhaps we should consider going back.

282
00:19:11,440 --> 00:19:12,270
Your call.

283
00:19:12,940 --> 00:19:14,058
Let me think, then.

284
00:19:15,660 --> 00:19:16,490
Over there!

285
00:19:16,760 --> 00:19:18,840
Something is moving extremely fast!

286
00:19:23,020 --> 00:19:24,620
That is definitely him.

287
00:19:24,880 --> 00:19:28,557
Although, he's nearing the
Imperial Capital's defenses.

288
00:19:28,640 --> 00:19:32,297
If we cross into their land, we
will not make it back in one piece.

289
00:19:32,380 --> 00:19:34,357
Right now, we are still
concealed from them.

290
00:19:34,440 --> 00:19:36,840
Once they become aware of our presence,

291
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:40,197
the magic will of course
immediately lose its effectiveness.

292
00:19:40,280 --> 00:19:43,398
That's true, but letting
him escape is not an option.

293
00:19:44,400 --> 00:19:48,957
They have powerful magical tools and can
use them to reinforce their military power.

294
00:19:49,040 --> 00:19:52,334
We cannot give them any
opportunity to make that happen.

295
00:19:55,280 --> 00:19:57,220
Of course, he's right.

296
00:19:57,500 --> 00:19:59,120
We are already at war.

297
00:20:00,500 --> 00:20:03,717
So, we have no idea what awaits us.

298
00:20:03,800 --> 00:20:04,740
Lord Rain,

299
00:20:05,020 --> 00:20:07,440
Lady Lindbergh, if I may,

300
00:20:07,680 --> 00:20:11,445
I would like you to grant me
permission to obliterate this area.

301
00:20:12,360 --> 00:20:13,190
Obliterate?

302
00:20:13,360 --> 00:20:15,797
If this is going to be
our escape route later,

303
00:20:15,880 --> 00:20:20,468
then it would be smart to take out the
defenses while we have the opportunity.

304
00:20:20,900 --> 00:20:25,220
In normal situations, Ines would
never suggest exerting her own power.

305
00:20:25,480 --> 00:20:28,380
But she is just as
angry as the rest of us.

306
00:20:28,580 --> 00:20:32,497
The royal capital she vowed to risk
her life to protect has been flattened.

307
00:20:32,580 --> 00:20:33,410
I agree.

308
00:20:33,493 --> 00:20:36,400
Do as you please, Inez,
and do not hold back.

309
00:20:36,820 --> 00:20:38,040
As you wish.

310
00:20:43,100 --> 00:20:44,300
Divine sword!

311
00:21:02,580 --> 00:21:03,460
Oh, well.

312
00:21:05,820 --> 00:21:09,232
I believe that will secure our
escape route, Your Majesty.

313
00:21:09,720 --> 00:21:10,550
All right.

314
00:21:10,633 --> 00:21:11,740
Very well done, Ines.

315
00:21:12,400 --> 00:21:13,230
Lynne!

316
00:21:14,100 --> 00:21:17,276
Our actions here will determine
the course of the war.

317
00:21:17,680 --> 00:21:21,777
We are going to keep pursuing the Emperor
all the way to the Imperial Capital.

318
00:21:21,860 --> 00:21:23,837
Are you sure you're ready for this?

319
00:21:23,920 --> 00:21:24,750
Yes.

320
00:21:27,440 --> 00:21:30,264
Everyone here wields power
far outside the norm.

321
00:21:30,920 --> 00:21:33,332
They are the strongest people imaginable.

322
00:21:34,140 --> 00:21:36,680
There is no need to worry about anything.

323
00:21:38,160 --> 00:21:41,720
Plus, above all, we have Sir Noor.

324
00:21:42,460 --> 00:21:45,740
I cannot even begin to
comprehend his greatness.

325
00:21:46,280 --> 00:21:49,460
Even now, he quietly
listens to all around him.

326
00:21:49,640 --> 00:21:51,934
And he knows the weight of this moment.

327
00:21:52,700 --> 00:21:55,377
We shall teach them a
hard lesson about what

328
00:21:55,460 --> 00:21:58,048
happens when you mess
with the wrong people.

329
00:22:10,180 --> 00:22:12,860
Thank you.

330
00:23:08,300 --> 00:23:11,100
Thank you.
